      "title": "Wildlife damages crops as sunflower dryer burns in Poland",
      "content_html": "Farmers in Poland’s Pęcław municipality say beaver burrows and dams are damaging Oder flood embankments, fields and drainage channels, renewing fears about levee safety after the 2024 flood. Separately, wild boars trampled an estimated 50% to 60% of a 2.5-hectare maize field near Aleksandrów Kujawski despite fencing. The farmer said homes within 150 metres limited hunting.\n\nA sunflower-seed dryer caught fire on Oct. 30 in Białowieża in the Opole region. Six units from the Nysa County State Fire Service responded, along with units from the Kamiennik and Lipniki volunteer fire services. The fire nearly destroyed the dryer and its load of sunflower seeds, but firefighters saved nearby farm buildings and a grain store. Firefighters suspect a fault during drying. Losses had not yet been reported.",
