      "title": "Trump says U.S. may strike remaining Iran targets; Tehran warns of retaliation",
      "content_html": "President Donald Trump said Oct. 31 that the United States may strike one or two remaining targets in Iran, naming the suspected underground nuclear complex at Pickaxe Mountain. Iran’s government denies conducting nuclear work there. Iran’s Supreme Leader Mojtaba Khamenei warned that any new U.S. or Israeli attack would draw an immediate response without geographic limits, while Secretary of State Marco Rubio said Trump had not decided whether to launch further strikes and Washington remained open to diplomacy.\n\nThe war began with U.S.-Israeli strikes on Iran on Feb. 28. Iran has restricted shipping through the Strait of Hormuz, and the disruption has driven up global energy prices. Qatar and Pakistan are mediating, and Vice President JD Vance sent a letter to Iran’s security chief Mohsen Rezaei. Iran’s Foreign Minister Abbas Araghchi said there were no plans for direct talks with U.S. officials.\n\nThe sides remain far apart on terms for ending the conflict, including Iran’s demand for the release of frozen assets. The United States holds midterm elections on Nov. 3, and Gulf officials told MS NOW they had been warned of possible U.S. strikes as early as Nov. 4. Rubio said no decision had been made.",
